## Claim
Text: "Joe Biden wants to ban fracking"
Claim author: The Donald Trump 2020 presidential campaign
Claim date: October 27, 2020

## Initial Q&A
### What was Joe Biden's official policy position on hydraulic fracturing (fracking) as stated in the Joe Biden 2020 presidential campaign platform?
Answer: According to the search result, Joe Biden's policy position was to "retain fracking" rather than ban it. Although the article notes that his past statements on the issue had been "confusing"—including previous debate assertions that fracking would be "eliminated" or that there would be "no more, no new fracking"—his 2020 campaign platform maintained that he would not ban the practice, with Biden repeatedly stating, "I am not banning fracking."

Source URL: https://www.newsweek.com/fact-check-does-joe-biden-support-green-new-deal-fracking-ban-1537291

### Did Joe Biden ever state during the 2020 presidential campaign that Joe Biden would completely ban hydraulic fracturing (fracking) in the United States?
Answer: According to the search result, Joe Biden did not state that he would completely ban fracking, and he explicitly declared, "I am not banning fracking." Although he did state "No more – no new fracking" during a March 2020 Democratic primary debate, his campaign subsequently clarified that "he meant he would not allow new federal land-drilling leases" rather than a complete nationwide ban on the practice.

Source URL: https://energynow.com/2020/09/the-biden-flip-flop-u-s-presidential-hopeful-biden-now-says-he-would-not-ban-fracking/

### Did Joe Biden distinguish between banning hydraulic fracturing (fracking) on public federal lands versus private lands during the 2020 presidential campaign?
Answer: Yes, during the 2020 presidential campaign, Joe Biden distinguished his position by repeatedly stating, "I am not banning fracking," while clarifying that he does support "stopping all 'oil drilling or gas drilling on federal lands.'"

Source URL: https://www.uagetinvolved.org/content/joe-biden-i-am-not-banning-fracking

### What did Joe Biden say about hydraulic fracturing (fracking) during the Democratic primary debates in 2019 and 2020?
Answer: During the Democratic primary debates, Joe Biden made statements opposing fracking that his campaign later had to clarify. In a July 2019 debate, when asked if there would be any place for fracking in his administration, Biden responded, "No, we would – we would work it out. We would make sure it’s eliminated and no more subsidies for either one of those..." Additionally, during a March 2020 debate, Biden stated that he was against "new fracking."

